## 11. Accessibility, fallback, mobile, and analytics contracts

### Accessibility

- Every interaction must have keyboard/touch/screen-reader parity.
- 44px minimum primary targets.
- Board keyboard move retains focus travel and live announcement.
- Cockpit is a real dialog: focus trap, Escape close, focus restoration.
- Onboarding is intentionally mandatory: Escape/outside click do not dismiss. “Just browsing” is the accessible low-friction choice.
- Reduced motion preserves state with immediate/crossfade behavior.
- No-JS keeps authoritative homepage/case links; onboarding bypasses.
- Forced-colors/Windows HCM still needs a real Windows pass after the recorded waiver.

### Mobile

- 320, 390, and 430 are first-class; 768/1024 medium layouts must avoid hero/dock collisions.
- Mobile board must remain fully discoverable via tablist/previous/next; drag is optional.
- 200% text at 320/390 must reflow without horizontal overflow.
- Neo Futurist cockpit panes stack on mobile.
- Both hero CTAs must remain visible and unmistakable.

### Analytics

- Five custom events only, plus PostHog pageviews/autocapture.
- `persona_selected` payload is currently typed as:

```ts
{
  persona: "founder" | "recruiter" | "product_lead" | "just_browsing";
  surface: "hero_onboarding";
  $set: { visitor_persona: samePersona };
}
```

- No custom event for scene transitions, guide reactions, board motion, funnel milestones, or cockpit open.
- Current-session funnel remains session-local/browser-local.
- Session recording remains disabled without a fresh explicit decision.

